00:14:27.400 --> 00:14:30.660
They were even given a commendation
for assisting in the arrest of a drug smuggler.

00:14:32.670 --> 00:14:35.870
That's it! The culprit might be someone
who has a grudge against them!

00:14:35.870 --> 00:14:37.910
That's true, it could be a grudge!

00:14:37.910 --> 00:14:40.270
There's a bar near here
where all the pilots hang out.

00:14:40.270 --> 00:14:42.280
I'll find out what I can about those two.

00:14:42.280 --> 00:14:42.480
What should I do?
I'll find out what I can about those two.

00:14:42.480 --> 00:14:43.110
What should I do?

00:14:43.110 --> 00:14:43.280
What should I do?
Keep an eye on the crybaby.

00:14:43.280 --> 00:14:44.650
Keep an eye on the crybaby.

00:14:44.650 --> 00:14:44.950
Arthur?
Keep an eye on the crybaby.

00:14:44.950 --> 00:14:45.280
Arthur?

00:14:45.280 --> 00:14:45.900
Arthur?
Yup.

00:14:46.050 --> 00:14:48.350
He's a naïve little boy, so he might...

00:14:48.650 --> 00:14:49.680
He might?

00:14:49.680 --> 00:14:51.390
He might blame himself and commit suicide.

00:14:51.390 --> 00:14:51.690
No way!
He might blame himself and commit suicide.

00:14:51.690 --> 00:14:52.210
No way!

00:14:56.320 --> 00:14:57.380
Arthur?

00:15:06.870 --> 00:15:07.860
Arthur!

00:15:11.640 --> 00:15:14.160
Higher! Higher!

00:15:19.850 --> 00:15:21.180
That's amazing!

00:15:21.180 --> 00:15:22.750
My computer controls it remotely.

00:15:22.750 --> 00:15:24.840
Oh, it's computer controlled?

00:15:25.020 --> 00:15:26.750
Yeah. I made them all.

00:15:27.190 --> 00:15:29.490
You seem to know a lot
about computers, Arthur.

00:15:55.780 --> 00:15:59.010
Let's see... Any open spots?

00:16:03.420 --> 00:16:03.860
Huh?

00:16:17.100 --> 00:16:19.700
It's the same number that
was on that spaceship.

00:16:26.110 --> 00:16:30.710
Crocker and Stablos?
When did they become so popular?

00:16:31.020 --> 00:16:31.950
What do you mean?

00:16:32.250 --> 00:16:36.250
Well, that beauty over there
was asking about them, too.

00:16:39.060 --> 00:16:41.820
Wow, she's as pretty as a picture.

00:16:48.240 --> 00:16:51.170
No way! She's the owner of that car?

00:16:52.370 --> 00:16:53.340
Oops...

00:17:14.000 --> 00:17:15.050
Don't move.

00:17:16.330 --> 00:17:17.630
Why are you following me?

00:17:17.930 --> 00:17:18.920
Who are you?

00:17:19.530 --> 00:17:21.090
Introduce yourself first.

00:17:21.170 --> 00:17:25.070
I'm an ASW accident investigator.
My name's Shannon Ross.

00:17:26.670 --> 00:17:28.110
Shannon Ross?

00:17:29.480 --> 00:17:30.640
So you're?

00:17:32.210 --> 00:17:35.340
If you're Eddie's wife, that means
you're Arthur and Melody's...

00:17:35.450 --> 00:17:36.750
Yes, I'm their mother.

00:17:36.750 --> 00:17:38.290
I didn't know...

00:17:38.290 --> 00:17:39.720
It's not your fault.

00:17:40.090 --> 00:17:42.180
You should have told me you were coming.

00:17:42.320 --> 00:17:45.130
Oh, really? Were you going to serenade
me with an orchestra when I arrived?

00:17:45.130 --> 00:17:48.400
You didn't even tell me about the accident.

00:17:48.400 --> 00:17:50.900
This accident is in my jurisdiction.

00:17:50.900 --> 00:17:52.300
It doesn't concern you.

00:17:52.570 --> 00:17:55.370
Melody is my child. It concerns me plenty.

00:17:55.370 --> 00:17:57.240
I can't leave this matter to you!

00:17:57.240 --> 00:17:58.730
There you go again...

00:17:59.210 --> 00:18:02.680
This wouldn't have happened to Melody
if you hadn't left in the first place.

00:18:02.680 --> 00:18:04.800
You're still talking about that?

00:18:04.980 --> 00:18:06.750
At any rate, stay out of it.

00:18:06.750 --> 00:18:08.910
I'll be the one to find Melody.

00:18:09.380 --> 00:18:13.720
Uh, I think it'd be much more efficient if we
worked together, instead of working separately...

00:18:14.390 --> 00:18:16.690
I'm going to do it my way.

00:18:17.660 --> 00:18:18.790
But...

00:18:18.790 --> 00:18:20.690
Aren't you going to see Arthur?

00:18:22.500 --> 00:18:24.020
He misses you.

00:18:24.970 --> 00:18:27.870
I need to find Melody first.

00:18:33.310 --> 00:18:34.210
Kei.

00:18:34.380 --> 00:18:34.710
Yes?

00:18:34.710 --> 00:18:34.980
You've been investigating the
pilots on Flight 807, haven't you?
Yes?

00:18:34.980 --> 00:18:38.570
You've been investigating the
pilots on Flight 807, haven't you?

00:18:38.710 --> 00:18:43.020
Yes. We thought someone might
have a grudge against the two pilots,

00:18:43.020 --> 00:18:49.250
but the drug smuggler was still in prison, and no
one else seems to have any problem with them.

00:18:49.360 --> 00:18:51.830
I see. Continue your investigation, then.

00:18:54.360 --> 00:18:57.060
What a frigid couple.
They're as cold as can be.

00:18:57.060 --> 00:18:59.130
I can understand how Arthur feels.

00:18:59.130 --> 00:19:00.260
Arthur?

00:19:00.640 --> 00:19:02.630
Yeah. Let's go visit him again.

00:19:04.140 --> 00:19:06.470
Are you saying Arthur's hiding something?

00:19:06.840 --> 00:19:08.510
Not really hiding something, but...

00:19:08.510 --> 00:19:13.240
...I think he might have something
to do with this kidnapping incident.

00:19:13.680 --> 00:19:17.520
You don't think Arthur's the culprit, do you?

00:19:17.520 --> 00:19:21.150
I don't think he is, but there's
something strange about him.

00:19:22.120 --> 00:19:25.890
All kids that age are a bit
emotionally unstable.

00:19:26.160 --> 00:19:29.130
About making 463 people vanish...

00:19:29.130 --> 00:19:31.860
I figured out a way to do that.

00:19:31.930 --> 00:19:35.230
Oh? So you know how to become
the greatest magician in the universe?

00:19:35.570 --> 00:19:38.940
Yes... And most likely, Arthur could do it.

00:19:38.940 --> 00:19:39.670
Huh?

00:19:53.950 --> 00:19:55.010
Arthur!

00:19:58.960 --> 00:20:00.620
Where are you going, Arthur?

00:20:00.700 --> 00:20:03.930
Not far. I'm going to
go play with my computer.

00:20:03.930 --> 00:20:06.800
You can play with that all you like later.

00:20:06.870 --> 00:20:09.770
Hey, why don't you come for a walk with us?

00:20:10.070 --> 00:20:11.270
But...

00:20:11.270 --> 00:20:13.310
Come on, just for a little bit.

00:20:13.310 --> 00:20:15.240
Yeah, it'll be a date.

00:20:15.240 --> 00:20:17.140
But I want to play with my computer...

00:20:17.140 --> 00:20:17.480
Oh, don't be like that.
But I want to play with my computer...

00:20:17.480 --> 00:20:19.050
Oh, don't be like that.

00:20:19.050 --> 00:20:20.450
Yeah, let's go.

00:20:21.420 --> 00:20:24.380
You see, Arthur, there's
something I want to ask you.

00:20:25.250 --> 00:20:25.450
Arthur!

00:20:25.450 --> 00:20:26.120
Watch out!
Arthur!

00:20:28.520 --> 00:20:29.550
Kei, are you all right?

00:20:29.890 --> 00:20:32.120
I am not all right! I hit my head!

00:20:37.330 --> 00:20:39.030
They're coming back! Dammit.

00:20:39.230 --> 00:20:40.390
They're persistent.

00:20:48.080 --> 00:20:49.840
Who are they?

00:20:49.940 --> 00:20:51.980
Not much for words, are they?

00:20:51.980 --> 00:20:53.950
They attacked without any warning.

00:20:53.950 --> 00:20:56.920
They're not good at talking,
but they sure are aggressive.

00:20:57.020 --> 00:20:58.890
I wonder who their target was?

00:20:58.890 --> 00:21:02.340
Who knows. It could have
been either of us, or...

00:21:03.090 --> 00:21:04.390
It couldn't be...

00:21:05.860 --> 00:21:10.350
Mama, Mama! These strangers
ruined your precious flower garden!

00:21:10.560 --> 00:21:12.500
Shoot, this is going to cost us!

00:21:12.600 --> 00:21:14.470
Think we can write it off
as a necessary expense?

00:21:14.470 --> 00:21:16.200
Look, look! See that mess?

00:21:16.200 --> 00:21:20.230
Ahh! How dare the two of you ruin my garden!

00:21:20.470 --> 00:21:22.240
What a pain. Better just run!

00:21:22.240 --> 00:21:23.940
You're right. Come on, Arthur!

00:21:30.790 --> 00:21:32.550
Don't you have something to tell us?

00:21:32.550 --> 00:21:35.590
Arthur, please tell us the truth.

00:21:35.590 --> 00:21:38.750
What happened earlier
wasn't a game of cops and robbers.

00:21:40.090 --> 00:21:41.290
He's not talking...

00:21:45.700 --> 00:21:47.220
It's another ransom note!

00:21:48.540 --> 00:21:49.800
What?!

00:21:49.900 --> 00:21:50.960
That's terrible!

00:21:51.410 --> 00:21:54.810
The ransom is now 46,300,000 credits?

00:21:54.810 --> 00:21:56.280
They increased it tenfold!

00:21:56.280 --> 00:21:57.380
No way...

00:21:57.380 --> 00:22:00.210
It's a lie! That's a fake!

00:22:00.210 --> 00:22:01.250
Arthur?

00:22:01.250 --> 00:22:02.880
What do you mean?

00:22:03.350 --> 00:22:05.690
It's not from the kidnappers! It's not!

00:22:05.690 --> 00:22:07.950
It's a fake! It's a fake!

00:22:08.160 --> 00:22:09.680
What's gotten into you, Arthur?

00:22:10.560 --> 00:22:13.360
It can't be from them! It can't be!

00:22:13.360 --> 00:22:14.850
There's no way!

00:22:14.930 --> 00:22:21.330
To Be Continued

00:22:43.320 --> 00:22:49.830
The mystery began after I fell asleep that time
Ano toki nemuri no ato ni okotta mistuerii

00:22:49.830 --> 00:22:56.300
I was guided by a voice from the future
Mirai kara kuru koe ni michibikareta no yo

00:22:56.300 --> 00:23:02.810
I passed through a distant, silvery time tunnel
Giniro haruka na taimu tonneru nukete

00:23:02.810 --> 00:23:09.480
And met a wanderer with unclouded eyes
Deatta sunda me no samayoibito

00:23:09.720 --> 00:23:11.850
Space Fantasy

00:23:11.850 --> 00:23:16.190
I came all this way just to meet you
Anata ni ai ni kokomade kita no

00:23:16.190 --> 00:23:18.360
Space Fantasy

00:23:18.360 --> 00:23:22.260
I came all this way just to meet you
Anata ni ai ni kokomade kita no

00:23:22.260 --> 00:23:28.740
Even if you were from another planet,
Tatoeba anata ga betsu no hoshi no hito demo

00:23:28.740 --> 00:23:35.110
It wouldn't matter to me, if I'd fallen in love
Watashi wa kamawanai aishita nara

00:23:35.780 --> 00:23:39.010
Dirty, Stormy Destiny

00:23:39.080 --> 00:23:41.720
Dirty, Stormy Destiny

00:23:41.720 --> 00:23:48.180
Love is zero G...
Koi wa mujuuryoku...

00:24:00.870 --> 00:24:03.170
Jeez, where'd they disappear to?

00:24:03.170 --> 00:24:05.760
Where are you? Stop hiding and come out.

00:24:06.210 --> 00:24:07.440
It's a mystery.

00:24:07.440 --> 00:24:07.710
Found you!
It's a mystery.

00:24:07.710 --> 00:24:08.140
Found you!

00:24:08.140 --> 00:24:08.340
Found you!
W-Where?!

00:24:08.340 --> 00:24:08.910
W-Where?!

00:24:08.910 --> 00:24:09.280
Under the sofa.
W-Where?!

00:24:09.280 --> 00:24:10.010
Under the sofa.

00:24:10.010 --> 00:24:10.810
Huh?

00:24:11.480 --> 00:24:13.550
A cat?! Get serious, already!

00:24:13.550 --> 00:24:15.480
What about the 463 people who vanished?!

00:24:15.480 --> 00:24:18.190
Leon, I was really worried
about you, you know.

